B.a9v=new A.cl("n01","A Tafel slope of 42 mV/dec | indicated a rate-determining | first electron transfer.")
B.a9s=new A.cl("n02","The (111) reflection at 2\u03b8 = 43.6\xb0 | broadened as | the crystallite size fell.")
B.a9o=new A.cl("n03","Scherrer analysis gave | a crystallite size of 8.4 \xb1 0.6 nm | for the calcined powder.")
B.a9N=new A.cl("n04","Extended X-ray absorption fine structure | resolved a Ni\u2013O coordination number | of 4.2.")
B.a9S=new A.cl("n05","A gas hourly space velocity of 24,000 mL/g/h | was held | for the entire run.")
B.a9O=new A.cl("n06","Sulfur was kept below 50 ppm | to avoid | irreversible poisoning.")
B.a9F=new A.cl("n07","Ostwald ripening coarsened the particles, | whereas encapsulation | suppressed coalescence.")
B.a9y=new A.cl("n08","The kinetics followed | a Mars\u2013van Krevelen mechanism | rather than Langmuir\u2013Hinshelwood.")
B.a9E=new A.cl("n09","The area-specific resistance rose | to 0.31 \u03a9 cm\xb2 | after five hundred hours.")
B.a9k=new A.cl("n10","Diffraction used Cu K\u03b1 radiation | with \u03bb = 1.5406 \xc5 | at room temperature.")
B.a9C=new A.cl("n11","The adsorption enthalpy \u0394H | was \u221278 kJ/mol | on the stepped facet.")
B.a9p=new A.cl("n12","Electrical conductivity reached | 3.6 \xd7 10\u207b\xb2 S/cm | after carbonisation.")
B.a9n=new A.cl("n13","Operando DRIFTS detected | a bridging carbonate band | at 1580 cm\u207b\xb9.")
B.a9M=new A.cl("n14","Isotopic labelling with \xb9\xb3CH4 | confirmed that lattice carbon | entered the product.")
B.a9u=new A.cl("n15","The reverse water-gas shift (RWGS) | consumed hydrogen | above 700 \xb0C.")
B.a9m=new A.cl("n16","NH3-TPD quantified | 0.42 mmol/g of | moderately strong acid sites.")
B.a9P=new A.cl("n17","BJH analysis showed | a bimodal pore distribution | centred near 4 and 19 nm.")
B.a9R=new A.cl("n18","Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy | produced a depressed Nyquist semicircle | on the aged electrode.")
B.a9G=new A.cl("n19","Rietveld refinement converged | with \u03c7\xb2 of 1.7 | and a weighted R-factor of 4.9%.")
B.a9A=new A.cl("n20","Single-atom alloys (SAA) | dissociated methane | without extensive coke formation.")
B.a9Q=new A.cl("n21","Multiwalled carbon nanotubes grew | from coordinatively unsaturated | nickel step edges.")
B.a9H=new A.cl("n22","The double-layer capacitance was | 28 \u03bcF/cm\xb2 | in one molar potassium hydroxide.")
B.a9K=new A.cl("n23","Selectivity toward ethylene | exceeded 71%, | whereas methane stayed below 3%.")
B.a9j=new A.cl("n24","Micrographs recorded at 200,000\xd7 | resolved lattice fringes | across the shell.")
B.a9U=new A.cl("n25","Pyrolysis proceeded at 5 \xb0C/min | under flowing argon | to 900 \xb0C.")
B.a9V=new A.cl("n26","The isotherm showed type IV hysteresis, | consistent with | high pore tortuosity.")
B.a9t=new A.cl("n27","Density functional calculations placed | the d-band centre | at \u22121.84 eV.")
B.a9L=new A.cl("n28","The Sabatier principle predicts | an optimum binding strength, | neither too weak nor too strong.")
B.a9g=new A.cl("n29","Anisotropic growth established | a percolating network | above 12 vol%.")
